---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A click-events table: 30 days, 400,000 rows a day. Change how it is stored and see how many bytes one query must read.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default query is <b>user_id, country, amount for the last 7 days where amount &gt;= 900</b> on a <b>columnar</b>, <b>partitioned</b> table. It reads only a few percent of the bytes a full row-format scan would, and no row group is skipped by statistics because the data is in arrival order.</li>
    <li>Tick <b>Data sorted by amount within each day</b>: the min/max statistics now rule out 49 of 56 row groups, so bytes read fall from 2.8% to 0.4% of the table. Switch <b>Layout</b> to <b>Row-oriented</b> and the same query reads every column of every row for the 7 days (23% of the table), with no row group skipping at all.</li>
    <li>Untick <b>Partition by day</b>: the query must open all 60 files and reads 12% of the table instead of 2.8%. Then set <b>Files per day</b> to 64: bytes only rise from about 122 MB to 155 MB, but the estimated time climbs from about 1.8 s to about 21 s because of the 1,920 small files (the small-files problem).</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg cf" data-cf>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Layout <select class="pg-in" data-layout><option value="col" selected>Columnar (Parquet-like)</option><option value="row">Row-oriented (Avro/CSV-like)</option></select></label>
      <label class="cf-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-part /> Partition by day</label>
      <label class="cf-check"><input type="checkbox" data-clustered /> Data sorted by amount within each day</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Query covers the last <b data-daysval>7</b> days <input type="range" min="1" max="30" value="7" data-days /></label>
      <label>Only amount &gt;= <b data-minval>900</b> <input type="range" min="0" max="1000" step="50" value="900" data-min /></label>
      <label>Files per day <select class="pg-in" data-files><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>4</option><option>8</option><option>16</option><option>32</option><option>64</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <fieldset class="pg-row cf-cols"><legend>Columns the query returns (amount is always read for the filter)</legend>
      <label class="cf-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-col="user" /> user_id</label>
      <label class="cf-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-col="country" /> country</label>
      <label class="cf-check"><input type="checkbox" data-col="payload" /> payload (120 B)</label>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="pg-row"><button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button></div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--accent)"><h3>Bytes read</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-bytes>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-bytesnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Files opened</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-filesopen>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-filesnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Row groups</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-rg>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-rgnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Estimated time</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-time>0</span><span class="pg-note">one worker, 100 MB/s plus 10 ms per file</span></div>
    </div>
    <canvas class="cf-canvas" data-canvas width="640" height="216" role="img" aria-label="Map of row groups: one line per day, oldest at the top"></canvas>
    <p class="pg-note cf-legend"><span class="cf-sw" style="--c: var(--accent)"></span> read <span class="cf-sw" style="--c: var(--role-2)"></span> skipped by min/max statistics <span class="cf-sw cf-empty"></span> day pruned by partitioning (never opened)</p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: compressed column sizes are 70% of raw for user_id, 15% for country, 50% for amount, 40% for payload and 5% for day; row-oriented files compress to 60% of raw; a file footer costs 16 KB plus 1 KB per row group. A columnar table has 8 row groups a day (more when there are more files). The full table is 30 days of 138 bytes a row. The engine reads whole column chunks of any row group it cannot skip.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  const DAYS = 30; const ROWS_DAY = 400000;
  const WIDTH: Record<string, number> = { user: 8, country: 2, amount: 8, payload: 120, day: 4 };
  const RATIO: Record<string, number> = { user: 70, country: 15, amount: 50, payload: 40, day: 5 };
  const ROW_RATIO = 60; const READ_BPS = 100000; const OPEN_MS = 10;
  const MIN_RGS = 8; // row groups per day at least
  const META = { file: 16384, rowGroup: 1024 }; // footer bytes read per file and per row group
  const AMOUNT_RANGE = 1000; // amounts run 0..999
  const UNSORTED_GAP = 10; // an unsorted row group's max amount sits within 10 of the top
  interface Params { layout: string; part: boolean; clustered: boolean; days: number; minAmt: number; files: number; cols: string[] }
  interface Plan { bytes: number; files: number; rgRead: number; rgStats: number; rgTotalScanned: number; ms: number; rgsPerDay: number; cells: number[][]; full: number }

  // integer hash of (a, b): prime mix, then the mulberry32 output mixer
  function hash(a: number, b: number) { let t = (a * 7919 + b * 104729 + 12345) >>> 0; t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0); }
  function rgsPerDay(files: number) { return Math.max(MIN_RGS, files); }
  // cells[day][rg]: 0 = read, 1 = skipped by statistics, 2 = day pruned
  function plan(p: Params): Plan {
    const R = rgsPerDay(p.files); const rows = ROWS_DAY / R; const first = p.part ? DAYS - p.days : 0;
    const cells: number[][] = []; let bytes = 0; let files = 0; let rgRead = 0; let rgStats = 0; let rgScan = 0;
    const rowWidth = Object.keys(WIDTH).filter((k) => k !== 'day').reduce((s, k) => s + WIDTH[k], 0);
    const cols = Array.from(new Set(['amount', ...p.cols, ...(p.part ? [] : ['day'])]));
    for (let d = 0; d < DAYS; d++) {
      const line: number[] = [];
      if (d < first) { for (let r = 0; r < R; r++) line.push(2); cells.push(line); continue; }
      files += p.files; bytes += p.layout === 'col' ? p.files * (META.file + META.rowGroup * (R / p.files)) : 0;
      for (let r = 0; r < R; r++) {
        rgScan++;
        let hi: number;
        if (p.clustered) hi = Math.floor((AMOUNT_RANGE * (r + 1)) / R) - 1; else hi = AMOUNT_RANGE - 1 - (hash(d, r) % UNSORTED_GAP); // sorted: each group covers a slice of the range; arrival order: every group spans almost 0 to 999
        if (p.layout === 'col' && hi < p.minAmt) { rgStats++; line.push(1); continue; }
        rgRead++; line.push(0);
        if (p.layout === 'row') bytes += Math.floor((rows * rowWidth * ROW_RATIO) / 100);
        else cols.forEach((c) => { bytes += Math.floor((rows * WIDTH[c] * RATIO[c]) / 100); });
      }
      cells.push(line);
    }
    const full = DAYS * ROWS_DAY * rowWidth * ROW_RATIO / 100;
    return { bytes, files, rgRead, rgStats, rgTotalScanned: rgScan, ms: Math.floor(bytes / READ_BPS) + files * OPEN_MS, rgsPerDay: R, cells, full };
  }
  function pct(a: number, b: number) { const v = (100 * a) / b; return v < 10 ? v.toFixed(1) : String(Math.round(v)); }
  function fmtBytes(n: number) { return n >= 1e9 ? (n / 1e9).toFixed(2) + ' GB' : n >= 1e6 ? (n / 1e6).toFixed(1) + ' MB' : (n / 1e3).toFixed(0) + ' KB'; }
  function fmtMs(n: number) { return n >= 1000 ? (n / 1000).toFixed(1) + ' s' : n + ' ms'; }
  function verdict(p: Params, r: Plan) {
    const share = pct(r.bytes, r.full);
    let s = `Reads ${share}% of the ${fmtBytes(r.full)} the table takes in row format. `;
    if (p.layout === 'row') s += 'Row-oriented files must be read whole: every column of every row in the days opened, and nothing can be skipped by statistics.';
    else if (r.rgStats > 0) s += `Statistics let the reader skip ${r.rgStats} of ${r.rgTotalScanned} row groups without reading any column chunk.`;
    else if (p.minAmt > 0) s += 'No row group can be skipped: in arrival order every row group holds both small and large amounts, so its min/max range always overlaps the filter. Sorting or clustering by amount is what makes statistics useful.';
    else s += 'The filter matches everything, so statistics cannot skip anything; only column pruning helps.';
    if (!p.part) s += ' Without partitioning the query cannot avoid any day.';
    if (r.files * OPEN_MS > 2 * (r.bytes / READ_BPS)) s += ' Time is now dominated by opening files, not by bytes.';
    return s;
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cf]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const canvas = q<HTMLCanvasElement>('[data-canvas]'); const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    let frame = 0;
    function read(): Params {
      return {
        layout: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-layout]').value, part: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-part]').checked, clustered: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-clustered]').checked,
        days: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-days]').value), minAmt: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-min]').value), files: Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-files]').value),
        cols: Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-col]')).filter((c) => c.checked).map((c) => c.dataset.col!),
      };
    }
    function css(name: string) { return getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue(name).trim() || '#888'; }
    function paint(r: Plan) {
      if (!ctx) return;
      const W = canvas.width; const H = canvas.height; ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      const rowH = H / DAYS; const colours = [css('--accent'), css('--role-2'), css('--surface-2')];
      const cw = W / r.rgsPerDay;
      r.cells.forEach((line, d) => line.forEach((v, i) => { ctx.fillStyle = colours[v]; ctx.fillRect(i * cw + 0.5, d * rowH + 0.5, Math.max(1, cw - 1), Math.max(1, rowH - 1)); }));
    }
    function draw() {
      frame = 0; const p = read(); const r = plan(p);
      q('[data-daysval]').textContent = String(p.days); q('[data-minval]').textContent = String(p.minAmt);
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-days]').disabled = !p.part;
      q('[data-bytes]').textContent = fmtBytes(r.bytes); q('[data-bytesnote]').textContent = `${pct(r.bytes, r.full)}% of the table in row format`;
      q('[data-filesopen]').textContent = String(r.files); q('[data-filesnote]').textContent = p.part ? `${p.files} per day for ${p.days} days` : `all ${DAYS} days opened`;
      q('[data-rg]').textContent = `${r.rgRead} read`; q('[data-rgnote]').textContent = p.layout === 'row' ? 'no statistics in row format' : `${r.rgStats} skipped of ${r.rgTotalScanned} in opened files`;
      q('[data-time]').textContent = fmtMs(r.ms);
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = verdict(p, r);
      canvas.setAttribute('aria-label', `Map of row groups, one line per day, oldest at the top: ${r.rgRead} read, ${r.rgStats} skipped by statistics, ${DAYS * r.rgsPerDay - r.rgTotalScanned} in pruned days.`);
      paint(r);
    }
    function schedule() { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(draw); }
    function reset() {
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-layout]').value = 'col'; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-part]').checked = true; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-clustered]').checked = false;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-days]').value = '7'; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-min]').value = '900'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-files]').value = '2';
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-col]').forEach((c) => { c.checked = c.dataset.col !== 'payload'; });
      schedule();
    }
    root.querySelectorAll('select, input').forEach((el) => { el.addEventListener('input', schedule); el.addEventListener('change', schedule); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', reset);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .cf-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .cf-cols { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .playground .cf-cols legend { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; padding: 0; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .playground .cf-canvas { width: 100%; max-width: 640px; height: auto; display: block; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--surface); margin: 8px 0; }
  .playground .cf-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 14px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .cf-sw { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--c); vertical-align: -2px; margin-right: 4px; }
  .playground .cf-empty { background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); box-sizing: border-box; }
</style>
